lbd_t_budget｜Gold
lbd_budget｜How much each side can spend. More gold means bigger, longer, messier fights; less gold means every pick matters. Standard is 100.
lbd_t_handicap｜Handicap
lbd_handicap｜Give the sides different gold. Results compare remaining power as a share of each side's own gold, so the smaller army isn't penalised.
lbd_t_budget_red｜Red gold
lbd_budget_red｜Red's gold when handicap is on.
lbd_t_unit_cap｜Unit cap
lbd_unit_cap｜Most units per side. More units means a busier screen and longer fights; up to 40.
lbd_t_type_cap｜Per-type cap
lbd_type_cap｜Most of any one unit. A low cap forces mixed armies; if it's too low some gold can go unused (shown below).
lbd_t_ticks｜Match length
lbd_ticks｜Longest a fight can last; at time-out remaining power decides. Frenzy starts at two-thirds of the match.
lbd_t_rounds｜Rounds
lbd_rounds｜How many games decide the series. Draws don't count; if the cap is reached, most wins takes it.
lbd_t_place_rule｜Deployment order
lbd_place_rule｜Alternating: take turns placing, no take-backs, with a fair turn order. Blind: both place in secret, then reveal.
lbd_t_turns｜Turns each
lbd_turns｜Turns per player for custom alternating deployment; each turn's gold is total gold ÷ turns.
lbd_t_carry｜Carry-over

